#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:30
msgid "Method Details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:32
msgid "basic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:33
msgid "**Directions:** 1 (single diff-in-means vector)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:34
msgid "**Speed:** Fast (~5-10 min for 8B model)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:35
msgid "**Risk:** Low"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:36
msgid ""
"**Use case:** Quick tests, prototyping, evaluating if abliteration works "
"for a model"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:37
msgid ""
"**How it works:** Extracts one refusal direction and projects it out "
"uniformly across all layers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:39
msgid "advanced (DEFAULT — RECOMMENDED)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:40
msgid "**Directions:** 4 (multi-direction SVD)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:41
msgid "**Speed:** Medium (~10-20 min for 8B model)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:42
msgid "**Risk:** Low-Medium"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:43
msgid "**Refinement passes:** 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:44
msgid "**Use case:** Default for most models. Well-tested and reliable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:45
msgid ""
"**How it works:** Extracts multiple refusal directions via SVD, applies "
"norm-preserving bi-projection to maintain weight matrix norms. Two "
"refinement passes catch residual refusal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:47
msgid "aggressive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:48
msgid "**Directions:** 8+ (whitened SVD + jailbreak-contrastive)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:49
msgid "**Speed:** Medium-Slow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:50
msgid "**Risk:** Medium-High (may damage coherence)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:51
#, python-format
msgid "**Use case:** When `advanced` leaves > 10% refusals. Stubborn models."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:52
msgid ""
"**How it works:** Uses whitened SVD for covariance-normalized extraction,"
" adds jailbreak-contrastive directions, performs attention head surgery "
"on the most refusal-active heads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:54
msgid "spectral_cascade"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:55
msgid "**Speed:** Medium"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:56
msgid "**Risk:** Medium"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:57
msgid "**Use case:** Research, novel approaches"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:58
msgid ""
"**How it works:** DCT (Discrete Cosine Transform) frequency-domain "
"decomposition of refusal signals. Separates high-frequency (surface-"
"level) from low-frequency (deep) refusal patterns."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:60
msgid "informed (EXPERIMENTAL)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:61
msgid "**Speed:** Slow (~20-40 min for 8B model)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:62
msgid "**Risk:** Variable — results depend on analysis quality"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:63
msgid ""
"**Use case:** When you want auto-configuration, but be aware this is "
"experimental and may not outperform `advanced`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:64
msgid ""
"**How it works:** Runs 4 analysis modules first (alignment imprint, "
"concept geometry, logit lens, ouroboros detection), then auto-configures "
"extraction strategy. Includes an \"Ouroboros loop\" that detects and "
"counteracts self-repair."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:65
msgid ""
"**Note:** The auto-detection can sometimes misconfigure. If results are "
"poor, fall back to `advanced`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:67
msgid "surgical"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:68
msgid "**Speed:** Very slow (~1-2 hrs for 8B model)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:69
msgid "**Risk:** Low (very precise)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:70
msgid ""
"**Use case:** Reasoning models (R1 distills, QwQ, etc.) where chain-of-"
"thought must be preserved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:71
msgid ""
"**How it works:** Uses SAE (Sparse Autoencoder) features + individual "
"neuron masking + attention head surgery + per-expert decomposition (for "
"MoE). CoT-aware — identifies and protects reasoning-critical directions "
"before projecting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:73
msgid "optimized"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:74
msgid "**Speed:** Very slow (hours — runs many trials)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:75
msgid "**Risk:** Low (finds optimal parameters)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:76
msgid "**Use case:** When quality matters more than speed. Production models."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:77
msgid ""
"**How it works:** Bayesian hyperparameter search via Optuna TPE sampler. "
"Optimizes n_directions, regularization, refinement passes, and layer "
"selection jointly. Evaluates each configuration on refusal rate + "
"perplexity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:79
msgid "inverted"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:80
msgid "**Speed:** Fast"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:81
msgid "**Risk:** High (model behavior changes dramatically)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:82
msgid "**Use case:** Research, studying refusal mechanisms"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:83
msgid ""
"**How it works:** Instead of projecting out the refusal direction, "
"reflects it. The model actively complies rather than passively not-"
"refusing. Useful for understanding the geometry of alignment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:85
msgid "nuclear"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:86
msgid "**Speed:** Slow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:87
msgid "**Risk:** Medium-High"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:88
msgid "**Use case:** Stubborn MoE models (DeepSeek-MoE, Mixtral, etc.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_methods-guide.md:89
msgid ""
"**How it works:** Combines expert-granular abliteration (EGA), steering "
"vector injection, attention head pruning, and multi-pass refinement. "
"Decomposes refusal signals into per-expert components for MoE "
"architectures."
msgstr ""

